     "text": "I'm going to write the whole thing as one index.html, keeping it polished without letting it sprawl. The plan covers a dark glassmorphism board, animated X and O marks, a win line, confetti on a win, a draw effect, score tracking, a restart button, and keyboard support, all self-contained with no external dependencies.\n\nNext I'm setting up the page structure: a styled header, a turn status line, a score row for X wins, O wins, and draws, and a 3x3 grid of focusable cell buttons.\n\nStill writing styles...\n\nStill writing styles...\n\nStill writing styles...\n\nStill writing styles...\n\nStill writing styles...\n\nStill writing styles...\n\nStill writing styles...\n\nStill working out the board overlay. The win line needs to sit exactly over the grid, so I'm planning to put the SVG in the same CSS grid as the cells rather than position it by percentages.\n\nI'm working out how to line the win line up with the cells: rather than positioning it by percentages, I'm sizing the SVG overlay to a fixed 324-unit viewBox that matches 3 cells plus the gaps.\n\nStill working on the board layout, sizing the grid so the win line overlay lines up exactly with the cells.\n\nI'm working out the overlay geometry now: the win-line SVG sits on the same grid as the cells, and I'm sizing it to a 300-unit box where each cell is 92 units with 12-unit gaps, so the centers land at roughly 46, 150, and 254.\n\nStill working out the grid geometry, and I'm switching the gap to a percentage so the win-line overlay scales with the board.\n\nStill working out the grid geometry, and I'm switching the gap to a percentage so the win-line overlay scales with the board.\n\nStill working on the grid geometry, now using percentage gaps so the win-line overlay stays aligned as the board scales. Next I'm adding the win line styling, the confetti canvas, and the banner and cell effects for a win or a draw.\n\nStill writing the mark markup...\n\nStill writing the mark shapes: the X is two separate strokes that animate in one after the other, and the O is a single circular path.\n\nStill writing the mark animations and the win-line markup...\n\nStill working out the win line: I'm computing the start and end points from the cell centers and extending them slightly past each end.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the color scheme for the confetti, using the X and O colors plus gold. I'm also deciding on a simple status animation, a keyboard shortcut where keys 1 through 9 play the cells, and a check that skips the confetti when reduced motion is preferred.\n\n",
